  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Derisking wastewater sector in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The World Bank is the lead GCF AE with UNIDO and UN-Habitat as Executing Entities. Water security is GCF&apos;s focal result area, which holds important potential to drive a paradigm shift in climate mitigation and adaptation efforts. The vision for this paradigm shift is to secure water resilience and water services under increased climate change impacts.  The project aims to both mitigate GHG emissions and build adaptive capacities in one project to derisk the wastewater sector located in climate hazard areas by capitalising on a partnership of UNIDO (industrial wastewater), UN-Habitat (municipal wastewater), and World Bank (policy, tariff, national scale-up, investment) in Thailand. The project aims to derisk and expedite the paradigm shifts of the wastewater sector in Thailand to be adaptive to climate change, leading water reclamation to reduce water tension between industrial and municipality uses through provisions of i) sustainable finance mechanisms tailored to the wastewater sector and ii) climate-resilient wastewater infrastructure in climate-vulnerable areas. Industries and communities located in coastal areas are proposed for the initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
